  <language>fr_FR</language>
  <keyword>nanmedian</keyword>
  <short_description>Mediane en ignorant les valeurs NaN.</short_description>
  <syntax>
    <syntax_item>m = nanmedian(X)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>m = nanmedian(X, dim)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>m = nanmedian(X, vecdim)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>m = nanmedian(X, 'all')</syntax_item>
  </syntax>
  <description>
    <p><b>nanmedian</b> calcule la mediane apres suppression des valeurs <b>NaN</b> dans chaque tranche traitee.</p>
    <p>La dimension par defaut est la premiere dimension non singleton.</p>
  </description>
  <examples>
    <example_item>
      <example_item_type>nelson</example_item_type>
      <example_item_description />
      <example_item_data runnable="cli"><![CDATA[X = magic(3);
X([1 6:9]) = NaN;
m = nanmedian(X, 2)]]></example_item_data>
    </example_item>
  </examples>
  <see_also>
